{
  "contract": "KRI-1170 slide tilt zoom, extends slide-tilt-parity v1. zoom (0.5..3, 1 = as framed, the default) scales the MEDIA about the CANVAS centre BEFORE it turns: media = (cropped photo region scaled cover for Fill / whole for Fit) x zoom, then every v1 rule applies to that size (rotated_bounds, corners, covers_canvas). A tilt at 0 degrees and zoom 1 is stored as no tilt; zoom 1 is left out of the stored tilt, so a tilt stored before zoom existed is byte-identical. zoom is a number in [zoom_min, zoom_max]. Only the media zooms: text, ink, stickers and the watermark stay put above it. Tolerance 1e-6.",
  "version": 2,
  "caps": {
    "zoom_min": 0.5,
    "zoom_max": 3.0,
    "protocol": 33
  },
